# #!/usr/bin/env python3
# """
# main.py — ETF BUY ADVISOR (cheapest-first)
# ==========================================
# Ranks every enabled ETF from cheapest to priciest and tells you which one to
# buy. It does not place orders.

# THE RULE
#   1. Score every ETF on CHEAPNESS (0-100, higher = cheaper)
#   2. Rank 1 = cheapest
#   3. If rank 1 is already more than MAX_WEIGHT_PCT of your portfolio,
#      skip it and go to rank 2. Keep walking down until one passes.

# HOW CHEAPNESS IS MEASURED
#   Each ETF is scored against ITS OWN history, never against the other ETFs.
#   That matters: small-caps and Nasdaq routinely sit 6-10% below a recent
#   high while Nifty 50 and gold rarely do, so ranking on raw drawdown would
#   just pick the most volatile ETF every single week.

#   Two components, both percentile ranks, both 0-100:

#     A. PRICE POSITION - where does the live price sit inside its own
#        trailing 1-year range of closes? 0 = at its 52-week low.
#        Cheapness contribution = 100 - price_percentile

#     B. DIP UNUSUALNESS - today's drawdown from its 50-day high, ranked
#        against its own past year of drawdowns. 90 means "this dip is
#        deeper than 90% of the dips this ETF normally has."
#        Cheapness contribution = drawdown_percentile

#     cheapness = (A + B) / 2

#   A score of 75 means the same thing for gold as it does for small-caps.
#   No weights to tune, no assumption that returns are normally distributed.

# SETUP
#   pip install growwapi pandas pyotp python-dotenv
#   export GROWW_TOTP_TOKEN="..."     # your API key / approval token
#   export GROWW_TOTP_SECRET="..."    # your TOTP secret
#   python main.py
# """

